+# 2026-09-25: Fleet PRE ocean-eligibility fail-closed gate (FACTORY_REGRESSION)
+
+Task: fix the confirmed factory regression reported in the OCEAN protected integration checkpoint (issue #80, 2026-09-25): current master `fleet-pre-exact-sha.yml` "Ocean merge eligibility" certified cert-SHA==head but did NOT fail on independent PR review verdict or on base≠master. It was observed as SUCCESS coexisting with `independent-review`=FAILURE and stale bases on #278/#289/#295/#298/#291.
+
+Why: a stale-base or review-failed candidate must never be certified READY_FOR_OCEAN at the exact head; that empty gate allowed Ocean-eligible status to appear alongside blocked candidates and undermined the independent review enforcement boundary.
+
+Current state: protected LKG / current default HEAD = `809b0292b26edb1ea320e61144f1b1dfed772922`. The gate step only ran `test "$CERTIFIED" = "$EXPECTED"` and echoed READY_FOR_OCEAN. No PR base check, no master-freshness check, no check of the `World Independent Adversarial Review` verdict on the exact head.
+
+Target state: the same single "Ocean merge eligibility" job fails closed unless ALL hold at the exact head: (1) fleet-pre certification equals the exact head SHA, (2) PR base ref is master, (3) the head is not behind current master (behind_by==0), (4) the `World Independent Adversarial Review` check on the exact head concludes `success` (pull_request events).
+
+Files / systems involved: `.github/workflows/fleet-pre-exact-sha.yml`, new `scripts/ocean-eligibility-gate.cjs` (pure decision + CLI), new `test/ocean-eligibility-gate.test.js` (fixture matrix + workflow regression guard), WORK_IN_PROGRESS.md.
+
+Known risks: adding a real review requirement may surface as failed "Ocean merge eligibility" on in-flight PRs whose independent review passes are pending/inconclusive (infra #290 prerequisite) — that is the intended fail-closed signal, not a new defect. Dispatch runs (non-PR) enforce SHA certification + freshness only; review PASS is required for PR merge decisions.
+
+Golden systems preserved: single existing gate (no parallel gate created), denial-of-final without independent review PASS, exact-SHA propagation, CI/test suite untouched.
+
+Errors that must not return: cert-SHA==head as the only condition; READY_FOR_OCEAN on a stale base; READY_FOR_OCEAN without independent adversarial review PASS at the exact head; fabricated PASS.
+
+Exact patch / change plan: (1) add a pure `evaluateOceanEligibility` decision (missing input fails closed), (2) wire the workflow to resolve trusted master, ahead/behind via compare API, and the review check via check-runs on the exact head, then call the script, (3) add the fixture-matrix + workflow-text regression test.
+
+Tests to run: `node scripts/check-js.js`, `node --test test/ocean-eligibility-gate.test.js`, `node --test test/independent-review-workflow.test.js`, `git diff --check`; full `npm run check` + PR CI in cloud.
+
+Deployment / PR plan: branch `ai/opencode/fleet-pre-gate-fail-closed`, one owned PR into master, no merge/deploy by this slice.
+
+Progress: implemented.
+
+Next action: bounded local verify, commit, push, open PR; independent review PASS stays an external prerequisite to merge.
+
+Completion criteria: focused tests green locally and in PR CI; the gate demonstrably BLOCKs stale base / failed review / stale certificate; no accepted metric regresses.
+
+---
